<p class="{{ $class ?? '' }}">Local Goods turns a staff perk into business for the independent shops around the office. Employers in Washington, DC's Golden Triangle district buy credits for their staff, and those credits can only be spent at approved local cafés, restaurants and shops in the district, never at chains. Employees get lunch or coffee on the company, small businesses get new customers from the office towers next door, and a district could see how much is being spent in its neighborhood. Why trust it: the money an employer puts in is held for them and their staff until it's spent, kept apart from Local Goods' own money, and a check on every transaction confirms the books still cover what's been promised. No one can spend more than they were given. An AI flags unusual payments, and a person decides each one. It's a working prototype, running on Stripe's test mode with no real money, built and tested in the open.</p>
